The storefront wishlist page for story 02-app is in place on the existing Pages Router, and the Jest suite passes.

Signed-in shoppers can open `/wishlist`, see saved items, and remove one so it drops off the list. A discontinued product shows its discontinued message. Guests are sent to `/login?returnUrl=/wishlist`. The header shows a Wishlist link only after sign-in, and the product page has an Add to Wishlist button next to Add to cart. Auth follows the storefront session (`/authentication`) and still accepts an `access_token` when one is stored. Requests go to `/api/customer/storefront/wishlist`, the same prefix the profile and cart clients use.

`npm test` in `storefront`: 2 suites, 8 tests, all passed. ESLint on the touched files reported only an existing `useMemo` warning in `ProductDetails.tsx`. I could not click through the running app; the full storefront stack is not up here.

